## Build with blocks. Connect to the real world.

SHAPE is a visual programming environment for robotics and IoT,
built on Google Blockly.

Create application logic by connecting blocks, integrate devices
and services, and use local language models through Ollama.
Run SHAPE locally on compatible hardware.

## What you can build

| Integration | What you can do |
| :--- | :--- |
| **ROS 2** | Connect visual application logic to ROS 2 applications. |
| **MQTT** | Exchange messages with connected devices and IoT services. |
| **REST APIs** | Connect applications to external services. |
| **Ollama** | Use language models running locally. |
| **Tactigon GEAR** | Add voice and gesture interaction to your applications. |

## Quick start

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Developer review required before merge**
>
> The following first-run options are drafts.
> Test them on a clean Ubuntu installation and publish only
> the validated procedure, including its prerequisites.

### 1. Get the project

```bash
git clone https://github.com/TactigonTeam/Tactigon-Shape.git
cd Tactigon-Shape
```

### 2. Start SHAPE

<details open>
<summary><strong>⚠️ Option A — Direct start · To verify</strong></summary>

Run from the repository directory:

```bash
bash start.sh
```

</details>

<details>
<summary><strong>⚠️ Option B — Configure the graphical session · To verify</strong></summary>

First check whether `~/.xprofile` already exists.

If it exists, merge the required settings instead of overwriting it.
Otherwise:

```bash
cp .xprofile ~/.xprofile
bash start.sh
```

**Developer check:** confirm whether this configuration is required
and whether the user must sign out and back in before starting SHAPE.

</details>

### 3. Open the interface

Once the application is running, open:

**http://localhost:5123**

> [!NOTE]
> Confirm the browser address during the clean-install test.
> Remove these review notices and the unused installation option
> before merging.

